        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>The Selous Game Reserve (now Nyerere National Park) is one of the largest protected wilderness areas on Earth, covering over 30,000 square kilometers of pristine African wilderness. Just a 45-minute flight from Zanzibar Airport brings you deep into prime big game country along the mighty Rufiji River.</p>
        <p>This 2-day fly-in safari delivers Tanzania's premier wildlife experience without long overland travel: open 4x4 game drives across palm savannahs, an exhilarating sunset boat safari among pods of hippos and basking Nile crocodiles, and an authentic overnight stay in a riverside tented camp beneath the southern stars.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="tour-section">
        <h2>Itinerary</h2>
        <div class="itinerary-timeline">
          <div class="itinerary-step" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-left: 1.5rem; border-left: 3px solid #0d6b5c;">
            <h3 style="color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Day 1: Zanzibar to Selous — Game Drive & Sunset Rufiji River Boat Safari</h3>
            <p style="color: #4e5d66; line-height: 1.6;">Morning private pickup from your Zanzibar hotel to Abeid Amani Karume International Airport (ZNZ). Board your 45-minute scheduled flight across the Zanzibar Channel, touching down directly at Mtemere Airstrip in Selous. Meet your dedicated safari guide in an open-sided 4x4 cruiser and head into the reserve for game viewing. Check into your riverside tented lodge for hot lunch and relaxation. At 3:30 PM, embark on a private sunset boat safari along the wide Rufiji River, encountering countless hippos, Nile crocodiles, and diverse waterbirds before returning for a bush dinner.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="itinerary-step" style="padding-left: 1.5rem; border-left: 3px solid #b8860b;">
            <h3 style="color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Day 2: Sunrise Game Drive & Return Flight to Zanzibar</h3>
            <p style="color: #4e5d66; line-height: 1.6;">Wake up to morning birdsong and tea/coffee before setting out on an early morning game drive during peak predator hunting hours. Track lions, leopards, giraffes, buffaloes, and rare African wild dogs around the lakes and watering holes. Return to camp for a full English breakfast, pack your bags, and enjoy a final game drive en route to the airstrip. Board your midday flight back to Zanzibar, arriving by early afternoon for private transfer back to your beach resort in time for sunset cocktails.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

